.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt FSTAT 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm fstat
.Nd stat a scheme-file handle
.Sh SYNOPSIS
See the
.Pa raven-abi
crate (syscall number 0x66).
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The .Nm system call is part of the scheme IPC protocol (see
.Xr scheme 7
and
.Pa architecture/03-system-servers.md ).
.Pp
For a filesystem handle,
.Nm
returns the 64-byte
.Vt Stat
record defined by
.Pa raven-proto-fs :
inode number, size, block count, timestamps, mode, link count and owner/group.
.Pp
Mode type bits come from
.Dv S_IFMT :
.Dv S_IFREG ,
.Dv S_IFDIR ,
.Dv S_IFLNK
and the device types.  Permission bits are stored and returned.  They are
.B not
enforced in this protocol version: there are no credentials on the wire and
.Dv uid
and
.Dv gid
are reported as zero.  Do not treat this as POSIX permission behaviour.
.Pp
A directory description has no `.` or `..` entries; the reader synthesizes
them.  The stat record does not expose the description's cursor.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Zero on success with the record written to the response buffer.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er -offset indent
.It Er EBADF
The handle is not a scheme-file handle.
.It Er EPROTO
The server returned a malformed record.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr open 2 ,
.Xr read 2 ,
.Xr write 2
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
